  "the_fault_as_seen": "every free-view stroke (stroke:1,2,4,5,6,7) lies on the view plane through the CURSOR, and the cursor never left the world origin (0,0,0) while the camera looked at targets 0.9–3.7 units up — so the free ink landed at floor level, in front of or behind the volume the hand was looking at, not in it. John: the shapes drawn in the volume are always in the floor; assume within a general volume of the space",
  "the_rule_to_pin": "the view plane passes through the volume the hand is working in: by default the camera TARGET (the centre of the view, which pans and orbits with the hand), and a cursor placed by shift+click sticks until reset. A hull occupies the volume its claims define; the ground bounds it only where a claim's feet reach it",
